Pyren is an original work (the Rust daemon in daemon/, the Tauri + SvelteKit
app in app/, and the OSD widget in osd/). Its fan and RGB modules were
written from scratch in Rust following the behaviour of the projects listed
below; no source code from them is copied into daemon/. This NOTICE records
third-party material and upstream credit, as required by GPLv3 section 5.


================================================================================
1. omen-fan-control  --  https://github.com/arfelious/omen-fan-control
================================================================================

Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later.

Used as the behavioural specification for:
  - daemon/crates/fan/           (fan control, curve, hysteresis, calibration)
  - daemon/crates/fan/src/cleaner.rs   (reverse-spin dust cleaner protocol)
  - daemon/crates/installer/     (driver + service installer, ported from the
                                  project's Python installer v2.0)

Also the origin of the vendored kernel driver tree in driver/ -- see section 3.


================================================================================
2. omen-rgb-linux  --  https://github.com/arfelious/omen-rgb-linux
================================================================================

Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later.

Used as the behavioural specification for:
  - daemon/crates/rgb/           (4-zone lightbar / keyboard RGB, the WMI
                                  command 0x20009 / type 11 "lightbar" dialect)

The porting review is in docs/04-rgb-porting-review.md. The per-key USB-HID
path was not ported. No files from this project are vendored.


