A handful of interface constants (numeric WMI command IDs and register
names such as HPWMI_MUX_MODE_*, HPWMI_SET_LIGHTBAR_COLORS, the rgb_zones
sysfs layout) are referenced in daemon/crates/{gpu,rgb} by name for
interoperability with this driver.


================================================================================
4. Runtime dependencies not distributed with Pyren
================================================================================

  - NVIDIA NVML / libnvidia-ml.so.1, and the nvidia-settings / nvidia-smi
    tools, are used by daemon/crates/overclock/ only if present: NVML is
    loaded with dlopen() at runtime and the tools are run as separate
    processes. No NVIDIA code is linked into or shipped with Pyren.
  - The acpi_call kernel module is loaded on demand; it is packaged
    separately by the distribution.

Rust and JavaScript build/runtime dependencies are under permissive licences
(MIT / Apache-2.0), compatible with the GNU GPL version 3.
